{"4483410": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Where You Were", "steam_appid": 4483410, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >CONCEPT</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>I’m still being haunted by the memories of a past life.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Where You Were</strong> is an atmospheric anomaly game about holding on to a memory as much as struggling to move on. It’s about documenting subtle changes that threaten to rewrite the memories you hold near and dear.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/db403811469f719d957aea23fb7ec3ca.poster.avif?t=1782752510\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/db403811469f719d957aea23fb7ec3ca.webm?t=1782752510\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/db403811469f719d957aea23fb7ec3ca.mp4?t=1782752510\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >MECHANICS</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Observe. Document. Capture.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Study the hallway carefully. Any changes, both major and subtle, must be recorded. Use your camera to capture the anomaly, and only by documenting all the anomalies can you restore the memory to its original form.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/c377caaaaefe1055ee3924931b917957.poster.avif?t=1782752510\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/c377caaaaefe1055ee3924931b917957.webm?t=1782752510\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/c377caaaaefe1055ee3924931b917957.mp4?t=1782752510\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FEATURES</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A subtle, psychological loop.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An atmospheric experience where horror stems from absence rather than presence.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An in-game camera mechanic that outputs beautiful Polaroid-like photos.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A haunting story told entirely through the environment and atmosphere.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >CONCEPT</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>I’m still being haunted by the memories of a past life.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Where You Were</strong> is an atmospheric anomaly game about holding on to a memory as much as struggling to move on. It’s about documenting subtle changes that threaten to rewrite the memories you hold near and dear.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/db403811469f719d957aea23fb7ec3ca.poster.avif?t=1782752510\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/db403811469f719d957aea23fb7ec3ca.webm?t=1782752510\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/db403811469f719d957aea23fb7ec3ca.mp4?t=1782752510\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >MECHANICS</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Observe. Document. Capture.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Study the hallway carefully. Any changes, both major and subtle, must be recorded. Use your camera to capture the anomaly, and only by documenting all the anomalies can you restore the memory to its original form.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/c377caaaaefe1055ee3924931b917957.poster.avif?t=1782752510\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/c377caaaaefe1055ee3924931b917957.webm?t=1782752510\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/extras/c377caaaaefe1055ee3924931b917957.mp4?t=1782752510\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FEATURES</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A subtle, psychological loop.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An atmospheric experience where horror stems from absence rather than presence.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An in-game camera mechanic that outputs beautiful Polaroid-like photos.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A haunting story told entirely through the environment and atmosphere.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "short_description": "Return to a fracturing memory with a camera in hand. Where You Were is a first-person psychological horror game of observation and absence. Study a changing hallway, photograph anomalies to hold the memory together, and capture the fragile pieces of a past you struggle to let go of.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4483410/30dbe8b9b9e07d36e6f88e354aaf0250f2b60543/header.jpg?t=1782752510", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstati